==Campaign ==
=== First round ===
The official campaign began on 19 November as the country's electoral commission announced the 12 candidates eligible to run. [[Andrija Hebrang (son)|Andrija Hebrang]] collected more signatures than any other candidate with over 140,000, [[Ivo Josipović]] was second with just under 120,000, [[Milan Bandić]] collected around 60,000, [[Vesna Pusić]] just under 50,000, while [[Dragan Primorac]] and [[Nadan Vidošević]] each collected over 30,000 signatures.<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.vecernji.hr/vijesti/u-utrku-pantovcak-ide-13-predsjednickih-kandidata-clanak-51025 | title=U utrku za Pantovčak ide 13 predsjedničkih kandidata | date=16 November 2009 | work=[[Večernji list]] | language=hr | access-date=14 December 2009 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20091119031719/http://www.vecernji.hr/vijesti/u-utrku-pantovcak-ide-13-predsjednickih-kandidata-clanak-51025 | archive-date=19 November 2009 | url-status=live | df=dmy-all }}</ref>  At the beginning of the campaign, most polls showed Josipović with a healthy lead over his opponents.<ref name="jutarnji-istrazivanje">{{cite web | url=http://www.jutarnji.hr/infografika---predizborno-istrazivanje/358708/ | title=Istraživanje | date=25 November 2009 | work=[[Jutarnji list]] | language=hr | access-date=14 December 2009 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20091123135312/http://www.jutarnji.hr/infografika---predizborno-istrazivanje/358708/ | archive-date=23 November 2009 | url-status=dead | df=dmy-all }}</ref> Although Hebrang held the second spot in most opinion polls during the summer,<ref>{{cite web | url=http://dnevnik.hr/vijesti/hrvatska/sokantni-rezultati-istrazivanja-sdp-potukao-hdz.html#video | title=Nikad veća razlika: SDP 'potukao' HDZ | date=1 August 2009 | work=[[Nova TV (Croatia)|Nova TV]] | language=hr | access-date=14 December 2009 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20091208092937/http://dnevnik.hr/vijesti/hrvatska/sokantni-rezultati-istrazivanja-sdp-potukao-hdz.html#video | archive-date=8 December 2009 | url-status=live | df=dmy-all }}</ref> he fell to as low as fifth place by November.<ref name="jutarnji-istrazivanje"/> He claimed opinion polls have never been kind to his party as most conservative voters refuse to participate in them and expressed conviction that come Election Day he will be the victor.<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.vecernji.hr/vijesti/hebrang-u-ankete-ne-vjeruje-ni-malo-dijete-clanak-59683 | title=Hebrang: U ankete ne vjeruje ni malo dijete | date=1 December 2009 | work=[[Večernji list]] | language=hr | access-date=14 December 2009 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20091213165721/http://www.vecernji.hr/vijesti/hebrang-u-ankete-ne-vjeruje-ni-malo-dijete-clanak-59683 | archive-date=13 December 2009 | url-status=live | df=dmy-all }}</ref> Despite Bandić's indecisiveness, he held second or third place in most polls during autumn.<ref name="jutarnji-istrazivanje"/> After he officially announced his campaign, most political observers expected him to get a bump in the polls, however that never materialized. After announcing his candidacy he continuously dropped in the polls, but still managed to claim second or third place.<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.jutarnji.hr/vesna-pusic-jaca-je-od-hebranga/405566/ | title=Vesna Pusić jača je od Hebranga | date=14 December 2009 | work=[[Jutarnji list]] | language=hr | access-date=14 December 2009 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20091216174310/http://www.jutarnji.hr/vesna-pusic-jaca-je-od-hebranga/405566/ | archive-date=16 December 2009 | url-status=live | df=dmy-all }}</ref> Nadan Vidošević led most polls during 2008 and early 2009, but never managed to take the lead after officially becoming a candidate.<ref>{{cite web | url=http://dnevnik.hr/vijesti/hrvatska/nadan-vidosevic-najpozeljniji-za-predsjednika-medzu-kandidatima-i-drazen-budisa.html | title=Nadan Vidošević najpoželjniji za predsjednika, među kandidatima i Dražen Budiša | date=3 September 2008 | work=[[Nova TV (Croatia)|Nova TV]] | language=hr | access-date=14 December 2009 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20100301010741/http://dnevnik.hr/vijesti/hrvatska/nadan-vidosevic-najpozeljniji-za-predsjednika-medzu-kandidatima-i-drazen-budisa.html | archive-date=1 March 2010 | url-status=live | df=dmy-all }}</ref>

Josipović based his campaign on the slogan 'Justice for Croatia' and kicked off his campaign with a rally in front of the [[Croatian National Theatre in Zagreb]]. He attacked the current Croatian government and the prime minister [[Jadranka Kosor]] for ignoring the needs of the little man and criticized her for not dealing with corruption.<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.javno.com/hr-hrvatska/foto--josipovic-snazno-zapoceo-sluzbenu-kampanju_282386 | title=Josipović snažno započeo službenu kampanju | date=19 November 2009 | work=[[Javno.com]] | language=hr | access-date=14 December 2009 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20100130085022/http://www.javno.com/hr-hrvatska/foto--josipovic-snazno-zapoceo-sluzbenu-kampanju_282386 | archive-date=30 January 2010 | url-status=dead | df=dmy-all }}</ref> Andrija Hebrang started the campaign with patriotic rhetoric with the slogan 'For a proud and European Croatia'.<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.vecernji.hr/vijesti/hebrang-ovo-je-postala-kampanja-krupnog-kapitala-clanak-66429 | title=Hebrang: Ovo je postala kampanja krupnog kapitala | date=14 December 2009 | work=[[Večernji list]] | language=hr | access-date=14 December 2009 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20091218102037/http://www.vecernji.hr/vijesti/hebrang-ovo-je-postala-kampanja-krupnog-kapitala-clanak-66429 | archive-date=18 December 2009 | url-status=live | df=dmy-all }}</ref> He praised Jadranka Kosor and her policies, mostly criticizing Dragan Primorac and Nadan Vidošević for abandoning their party, calling them deserters and traitors of their party. He argued that he offered Primorac and Vidošević an opportunity to settle the question of who will be their party's nominee for president through a primary challenge stating that they both refused.<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.zadarskilist.hr/clanci/10112009/hebrang-vidosevic-i-primorac-su-dezerteri | title=Hebrang: Vidošević i Primorac su dezerteri | date=10 November 2009 | work=[[Zadarski list]] | language=hr | access-date=14 December 2009 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20091118035838/http://www.zadarskilist.hr/clanci/10112009/hebrang-vidosevic-i-primorac-su-dezerteri | archive-date=18 November 2009 | url-status=live | df=dmy-all }}</ref>

[[File:Ivo Josipović Croatian National Theatre Zagreb.jpg|thumb|300px|A crowd listening to Ivo Josipović speak as he begins his campaign with a rally on [[Marshal Tito Square]] in Zagreb]]

Nadan Vidošević used his knowledge of economic issues to gain popularity during the [[2008 financial crisis]]. He emphasized his business success during the 1990s as well as his post as the president of the Croatian Economic Chamber (CEC).<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.index.hr/vijesti/clanak/vidosevic-najavljuje-kandidaturu-predsjednik-mora-braniti-hrvatsku-na-ekonomskom-planu/448280.aspx | title=Vidošević najavljuje kandidaturu: Predsjednik mora braniti Hrvatsku na ekonomskom planu | date=31 August 2009 | work=[[Index.hr]] | language=hr | access-date=15 December 2009 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20090904140109/http://www.index.hr/vijesti/clanak/vidosevic-najavljuje-kandidaturu-predsjednik-mora-braniti-hrvatsku-na-ekonomskom-planu/448280.aspx | archive-date=4 September 2009 | url-status=live | df=dmy-all }}</ref> However, the press continuously raised the subject of his estate and property and how was he able to amass such an enormous wealth in a short period of time.<ref>{{cite web | url=http://dnevnik.hr/vijesti/hrvatska/vidosevic-uvjerljivo-najbogatiji-predjsednicki-kandidat.html | title=Vidošević uvjerljivo najbogatiji predsjednički kandidat | date=10 September 2009 | work=[[Nova TV (Croatia)|Nova TV]] | language=hr | access-date=15 December 2009 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20110929103153/http://dnevnik.hr/vijesti/hrvatska/vidosevic-uvjerljivo-najbogatiji-predjsednicki-kandidat.html | archive-date=29 September 2011 | url-status=live | df=dmy-all }}</ref> He usually responded saying that everything he has he built with hard work and smart business moves.<ref>{{cite web | url=http://dnevnik.hr/vijesti/hrvatska/vidosevic-ni-lipu-nisam-zaradio-u-privatizaciji.html | title=Vidošević: Ni lipu nisam zaradio u privatizaciji | date=4 October 2009 | work=[[Nova TV (Croatia)|Nova TV]] | language=hr | access-date=15 December 2009 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20091209061747/http://dnevnik.hr/vijesti/hrvatska/vidosevic-ni-lipu-nisam-zaradio-u-privatizaciji.html | archive-date=9 December 2009 | url-status=live | df=dmy-all }}</ref> On 9 December Dragan Primorac accused Vidošević of nepotism and criminal, claiming that he employed three of his nephews in the CEC and that his secretary was related to him.<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.monitor.hr/clanci/nadan-vidosevic-u-hgk-i-krasu-zaposlio-tri-necaka/26550/ | title=Nadan Vidošević u HGK i Krašu zaposlio tri nećaka | date=19 November 2009 | work=[[Monitor.hr]] | language=hr | access-date=15 December 2009 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20091224001800/http://www.monitor.hr/clanci/nadan-vidosevic-u-hgk-i-krasu-zaposlio-tri-necaka/26550 | archive-date=24 December 2009 | url-status=live | df=dmy-all }}</ref> Vidošević responded by saying he does not need someone who hits women teaching him moral lessons referring to allegations made to Primorac long ago which claimed he beat his former partner.<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.javno.com/iz-minute-u-minutu/clanak.php?id=3050551 | title=Primorac tuži Vidoševića zbog priče da tuče žene! | date=14 December 2009 | work=[[Monitor.hr]] | language=hr | access-date=15 December 2009 | archive-date=21 November 2020 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201121143107/http://www.javno.com/iz-minute-u-minutu/clanak.php?id=3050551 | url-status=dead }}</ref> Primorac accused Vidošević of lying and threatened a lawsuit if he did not apologize to him and his wife.<ref name="primorac-vidosevic-exchange">{{cite web | url=http://www.index.hr/vijesti/clanak/rat-bivsih-hdzovaca-primorac-prijeti-vidosevicu-sudskom-tuzbom/465098.aspx | title=Rat bivših HDZ-ovaca: Primorac prijeti Vidoševiću sudskom tužbom | date=14 December 2009 | work=[[Index.hr]] | language=hr | access-date=14 December 2009 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20091217075917/http://www.index.hr/vijesti/clanak/rat-bivsih-hdzovaca-primorac-prijeti-vidosevicu-sudskom-tuzbom/465098.aspx | archive-date=17 December 2009 | url-status=live | df=dmy-all }}</ref> During a debate held on 10 December Primorac and Vidošević exchanged insults, Vidošević repeating his allegations and Primorac demanding an apology.<ref>{{cite web | url=http://izbori.dnevnik.hr/multimedia/vijesti | title=Sučeljavanje | date=14 December 2009 | work=[[Nova TV (Croatia)|Nova TV]] | language=hr | access-date=15 December 2009 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20091227103952/http://izbori.dnevnik.hr/multimedia/vijesti | archive-date=27 December 2009 | url-status=dead | df=dmy-all }}</ref>  Finally, on 14 December Primorac announced he will be pressing charges against Vidošević claiming he caused great emotional damage to him and especially his wife.<ref name="primorac-vidosevic-exchange"/>  Vidošević responded by saying Primorac would do anything to gain attention saying his campaign was falling apart.<ref name="primorac-vidosevic-exchange"/>

Milan Bandić avoided most debates saying he was a man of work, not of words.<ref name="bandic-ideology">{{cite web|url=http://www.nacional.hr/clanak/71835/covjek-iz-naroda-bandic-uvjeren-da-ce-pobijediti-vec-u-prvom-krugu |title=Čovjek iz naroda: Bandić uvjeren da će pobijediti već u prvom krugu |date=20 November 2009 |work=[[Nacional (weekly)|Nacional]] |language=hr |access-date=15 December 2009 |trans-title=People's person: Bandić confident of first round victory |archive-date=13 June 2011 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20110613172006/http://www.nacional.hr/clanak/71835/covjek-iz-naroda-bandic-uvjeren-da-ce-pobijediti-vec-u-prvom-krugu }}</ref>  Most political pundits, however, thought he was afraid of confronting the other candidates as he usually tends to perform badly in debates.<ref>{{cite web | url=http://business.hr/hr/Naslovnica/Politika/Zasto-Bandic-izbjegava-suceljavanje | title=Zašto Bandić izbjegava sučeljavanje? | date=11 December 2009 | work=[[Business.hr]] | language=hr | access-date=15 December 2009 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20091214022002/http://business.hr/hr/Naslovnica/Politika/Zasto-Bandic-izbjegava-suceljavanje | archive-date=14 December 2009 | url-status=dead | df=dmy-all }}</ref> He based his campaign on the message that he was just one of the people, not an intellectual, but an ordinary hardworking patriot.<ref name="bandic-ideology"/> Vesna Pusić heavily emphasized her gender in the campaign claiming it was time for a woman to make it to [[Presidential Palace, Zagreb|Pantovčak]].<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.index.hr/vijesti/clanak.aspx?id=460478 | title=Pusić: Žena drži barem tri ugla kuće, a vrijeme je za veliko pospremanje | date=17 November 2009 | work=[[Index.hr]] | language=hr | access-date=15 December 2009 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20121016183406/http://www.index.hr/vijesti/clanak.aspx?id=460478 | archive-date=16 October 2012 | url-status=live | df=dmy-all }}</ref>  Most commentators noticed she made the biggest change of image during the campaign out of all candidates claiming she lost her strict appearance of a professor becoming more accessible and open about her personal life.<ref>{{cite web | url=http://izbori.dnevnik.hr/clanak/andrija_hebrang/usred-kampanje-najveci-preokret-napravili-pusic-i-hebrang.html?&page=3&p_all_items=16 | title=Najveći preokret napravili Pusić i Hebrang | date=13 December 2009 | work=[[Nova TV (Croatia)|Nova TV]] | language=hr | access-date=15 December 2009 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20110721095958/http://izbori.dnevnik.hr/clanak/andrija_hebrang/usred-kampanje-najveci-preokret-napravili-pusic-i-hebrang.html?&page=3&p_all_items=16 | archive-date=21 July 2011 | url-status=dead | df=dmy-all }}</ref> She based her campaign on her liberal and pro-European positions as well as her foreign policy experience.<ref>{{cite web | url=http://metro-portal.hr/vijesti/hrvatska/vesna-pusic-o-prednostima-clanstva-u-eu | title=Vesna Pusić o prednostima članstva u EU | date=7 December 2009 | work=[[Metro-portal.hr]] | language=hr | access-date=15 December 2009 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20091208153735/http://metro-portal.hr/vijesti/hrvatska/vesna-pusic-o-prednostima-clanstva-u-eu | archive-date=8 December 2009 | url-status=live | df=dmy-all }}</ref>

The presentation of candidates on national television is customarily a contentious issue, with minor candidates complaining of lack of coverage and the major candidates complaining about dilution of campaign on fringe issues. [[Croatian Radiotelevision]], as the public television operator, is legally obliged to give each candidate equal airtime, and they all got a half-hour interview in the late prime-time political show ''"Otvoreno"''.<ref>{{cite web | url=http://predsjednicki-izbori.com/izdvojeno/zavrsno-suceljavanje-na-novoj-tv/ | title=Prvo "Nedjeljom u 2", pa se predomislili u korist "Otvorenog" | date=December 4, 2009 | language=hr | work=[[Novi list]] | access-date=December 16, 2009 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20091214110005/http://predsjednicki-izbori.com/izdvojeno/zavrsno-suceljavanje-na-novoj-tv/ | archive-date=December 14, 2009 | url-status=live | df=mdy-all }}</ref> There were three televised debates held in the first round.<ref name="debates-businesshr">{{cite web | url=http://business.hr/hr/Naslovnica/Politika/Nova-TV-pobijedila-HTV-u-borbi-za-suceljavanje-predsjednickih-kandidata | title=Nova TV pobijedila HTV u borbi za sučeljavanje predsjedničkih kandidata | date=19 November 2009 | work=[[Business.hr]] | language=hr | access-date=15 December 2009 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120227033757/http://business.hr/hr/Naslovnica/Politika/Nova-TV-pobijedila-HTV-u-borbi-za-suceljavanje-predsjednickih-kandidata | archive-date=27 February 2012 | url-status=dead | df=dmy-all }}</ref> The first was held on 20 November on [[Croatian Radiotelevision|HRT]] with 10 candidates present.<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.ezadar.hr/clanak/prvo-suceljavanje-predsjednickih-kandidata-u-svadalackom-tonu | title=Prvo sučeljavanje predsjedničkih kandidata u svađalačkom tonu | date=21 November 2009 | work=[[Ezadar.hr]] | language=hr | access-date=15 December 2009 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20091227011451/http://www.ezadar.hr/clanak/prvo-suceljavanje-predsjednickih-kandidata-u-svadalackom-tonu | archive-date=27 December 2009 | url-status=live | df=dmy-all }}</ref> Andrija Hebrang and [[Boris Mikšić]] refused to attend claiming they were discriminated on all [[Television in Croatia|national television networks]].<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.novilist.hr/Izbori/hebrang-optuzuje-htv-za--BBkroje.aspx | title=Hebrang optužuje HTV za "krojenje drugog kruga" | date=21 November 2009 | work=[[Novi list]] | language=hr | access-date=15 December 2009 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20091128023341/http://www.novilist.hr/Izbori/hebrang-optuzuje-htv-za--BBkroje.aspx | archive-date=28 November 2009 | url-status=dead | df=dmy-all }}</ref> The second was held on 10 December on [[Nova TV (Croatia)|Nova TV]] hosted by [[Mislav Bago]]. Five candidates that were ahead in the polls were present, Ivo Josipović, Nadan Vidošević, Andrija Hebrang, Dragan Primorac and Vesna Pusić. Milan Bandić refused to attend.<ref name="novatv-debate">{{cite web | url=http://videoteka.novatv.hr/multimedia/predsjednicka-utrka-prvo-suceljavanje-cijela-emisija.html | title=Predsjednička utrka – Prvo sučeljavanje | date=10 December 2009 | work=[[Nova TV (Croatia)|Nova TV]] | language=hr | access-date=15 December 2009 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20091215010804/http://videoteka.novatv.hr/multimedia/predsjednicka-utrka-prvo-suceljavanje-cijela-emisija.html | archive-date=15 December 2009 | url-status=live | df=dmy-all }}</ref> The main topics were the fight against corruption, the economy and the [[European Union]].<ref name="novatv-debate"/> A poll conducted after the debate showed Vesna Pusić won the debate with 30% of those polled responding she did best, with Ivo Josipović coming in second with 26%. The poll also showed Ivo Josipović was the most specific in his answers with Vesna Pusić following closely. The audience considered Nadan Vidošević the most likable and Andrija Hebrang the most entertaining.<ref>{{cite web | url=http://izbori.dnevnik.hr/clanak/vijesti/analiza.html | title=Sučeljavanje: Vesna Pusić ostavila je najbolji dojam | date=12 December 2009 | work=[[Nova TV (Croatia)|Nova TV]] | language=hr | access-date=15 December 2009 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20091215011740/http://izbori.dnevnik.hr/clanak/vijesti/analiza.html | archive-date=15 December 2009 | url-status=dead | df=dmy-all }}</ref> The final debate was once again held on HRT on 22 December and was the only one with all 12 candidates present. The main topics of discussion were campaign spending, corruption and the suggestion of removing political immunity.<ref>{{cite web | url=http://predsjednicki-izbori.com/tag/josip-jurcevic/ | title=Kandidati za predsjednika: održano posljednje sučeljavanje | date=23 December 2009 | work=Predsjednicki-izbori.com | language=hr | access-date=24 December 2009 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20091215032106/http://predsjednicki-izbori.com/tag/josip-jurcevic/ | archive-date=15 December 2009 | url-status=live | df=dmy-all }}</ref> There were four debates planned with the final one to be held on Nova TV on 23 December with six major candidates to be present.<ref name="debates-businesshr"/> However, the six candidates behind in the polls objected saying they were discriminated by Nova TV, particularly [[Josip Jurčević]] who threatened to sue the television station and filed a complaint against it to the country's electoral commission.<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.javno.com/hr-hrvatska/jurcevic-trazi-ukidanje-koncesije-novoj-tv_285163 | title=Jurčević traži ukidanje koncesije Novoj TV | date=7 December 2009 | work=[[Javno.com]] | language=hr | access-date=24 December 2009 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20091212131335/http://www.javno.com/hr-hrvatska/jurcevic-trazi-ukidanje-koncesije-novoj-tv_285163 | archive-date=12 December 2009 | url-status=live | df=dmy-all }}</ref> Finally, Nova TV canceled the scheduled debate and called for the change of Croatia's laws concerning media coverage of presidential campaigns.<ref>{{cite web | url=http://predsjednicki-izbori.com/vijesti/nova-tv-prisiljena-otkazati-emisiju-predsjednicka-utrka/ | title=Nova TV prisiljena otkazati emisiju 'Predsjednička utrka' | date=18 December 2009 | work=Predsjednicki-izbori.com | language=hr | access-date=24 December 2009 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20111009134146/http://predsjednicki-izbori.com/vijesti/nova-tv-prisiljena-otkazati-emisiju-predsjednicka-utrka/ | archive-date=9 October 2011 | url-status=live | df=dmy-all }}</ref>

