=== Second round ===
Immediately after the official results were published shortly after midnight 28 December and it was clear the two candidates to face in a runoff would be Josipović and Bandić all the major candidates gave their speeches. Josipović called for voters to vote for the light, not for the dark,<ref name="josipovic-light-dark">{{cite web | url = http://www.rtl.hr/josipovic-ja-sam-svjetlo-bandic-tama-video-5322 | title = Josipović: Ja sam svjetlo, Bandić tama | work = [[RTL Televizija]] | date = December 28, 2009 | language = hr | access-date = December 30, 2009 | archive-url = https://web.archive.org/web/20091230011347/http://www.rtl.hr/josipovic-ja-sam-svjetlo-bandic-tama-video-5322 | archive-date = December 30, 2009 | url-status = live | df = mdy-all }}</ref> while Bandić insulted Josipović saying he was a pawn of Zoran Milanović and nothing more than his remote-control.<ref name="bandic-pawn">{{cite web | url = http://www.rtl.hr/bandic-josipovica-stvorili-u-laboratoriju-video-5321 | title = Bandić: Josipovića stvorili u laboratoriju! | work = [[RTL Televizija]] | date = December 28, 2009 | language = hr | access-date = December 30, 2009 | archive-url = https://web.archive.org/web/20091230011548/http://www.rtl.hr/bandic-josipovica-stvorili-u-laboratoriju-video-5321 | archive-date = December 30, 2009 | url-status = live | df = mdy-all }}</ref> The following morning the official campaign for the second round began. Josipović denied being an SDP project calling himself independent and accusing Bandić of being a remote-control of [[Ivo Sanader]],<ref>{{cite web | url = http://www.javno.com/hr-hrvatska/bandic-je-sanaderov-daljinski-upravljac_287871 | title = Josipović: Bandić je Sanaderov daljinski upravljač | work = javno.com | date = December 28, 2009 | language = hr | access-date = December 30, 2009 | archive-url = https://archive.today/20130127005946/http://www.javno.com/hr-hrvatska/bandic-je-sanaderov-daljinski-upravljac_287871 | archive-date = January 27, 2013 | url-status = live | df = mdy-all }}</ref> referring among other things to claims by Dragan Primorac that Bandić was the favorite of the former [[Prime Minister of Croatia|prime minister]].<ref>{{cite web | url = http://izbori.dnevnik.hr/clanak/dragan_primorac/primorac-sanader-se-vraca-u-politiku-preko-bandica.html?&page=2&p_all_items=11 | title = Primorac: Sanader se vraća u politiku preko Bandića | work = [[Nova TV (Croatia)|Nova TV]] | date = December 12, 2009 | language = hr | access-date = December 30, 2009 | archive-url = https://web.archive.org/web/20110721100635/http://izbori.dnevnik.hr/clanak/dragan_primorac/primorac-sanader-se-vraca-u-politiku-preko-bandica.html?&page=2&p_all_items=11 | archive-date = July 21, 2011 | url-status = dead | df = mdy-all }}</ref><ref name="tportal-jutarnji-endorsements"/> Bandić denied the rumors, however the following day the media published a story claiming that Bandić and Sanader had a secret lunch that very day in a Zagreb restaurant. Bandić denied the rumors calling the journalists who published the story liars, saying the media's favorite is Josipović and that they would do anything to discredit him.<ref>{{cite web | url = http://www.index.hr/vijesti/clanak/tajni-rucak-s-odbjeglim-premijerom-bandic-i-sanader-sastali-se-u-restoranu-kamanjo/467553.aspx | title = Tajni ručak s odbjeglim premijerom: Bandić i Sanader sastali se u restoranu Kamanjo! | language = hr | publisher = Index.hr | date = December 29, 2009 | access-date = December 30, 2009 | archive-url = https://web.archive.org/web/20091231181052/http://www.index.hr/vijesti/clanak/tajni-rucak-s-odbjeglim-premijerom-bandic-i-sanader-sastali-se-u-restoranu-kamanjo/467553.aspx | archive-date = December 31, 2009 | url-status = live | df = mdy-all }}</ref>

On Monday 28 December, the first day of the runoff campaign, the incumbent [[President of Croatia|president]] [[Stjepan Mesić]] indicated that he supports Ivo Josipović to be his successor. He praised his manifesto and said Croatia needs a president working actively against corruption and for justice.<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.vecernji.hr/vijesti/predsjednik-mesic-rukavicama-podrzao-ivu-josipovica-clanak-72774 | title=Predsjednik Mesić u rukavicama podržao Ivu Josipovića | publisher=[[Večernji List]] | date=December 28, 2009 | access-date=December 30, 2009 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20091231021348/http://www.vecernji.hr/vijesti/predsjednik-mesic-rukavicama-podrzao-ivu-josipovica-clanak-72774 | archive-date=December 31, 2009 | url-status=live | df=mdy-all }}</ref> He also insulted Milan Bandić saying it was impossible he only spent 3&nbsp;million kuna for the campaign saying he knows how much a campaign costs. He pleaded for more transparency and called on him to release the names of those who were really financing his campaign. Bandić responded by saying that Mesić hasn't released the names of his donors to this day and that he was a part of both of his campaigns so he knows how nontransparent they were.<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.ipress.hr/hrvatska/bandic-prozvao-mesica-i-pozvao-ga-da-objavi-donatore-od-prije-10-godina-1469.html | title=Bandić prozvao Mesića i pozvao ga da objavi donatore od prije 10 godina | publisher=ipress.hr | date=December 28, 2009 | access-date=December 30, 2009 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20091230010520/http://www.ipress.hr/hrvatska/bandic-prozvao-mesica-i-pozvao-ga-da-objavi-donatore-od-prije-10-godina-1469.html | archive-date=December 30, 2009 | url-status=live | df=mdy-all }}</ref> Mesić called Bandić a liar saying he was the only one in those days to release the name of every single person who contributed to his victory. He said his campaign reports were published, on Croatian, not English, clearly referring to the fact that Bandić couldn't speak proper English.<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.vecernji.hr/vijesti/mesic-bandic-laze-bandic-mesic-je-malo-ostario-je-zaboravio-clanak-73129 | title=Mesić: Bandić laže; Bandić: Mesić je malo ostario, pa je zaboravio | publisher=[[Večernji List]] | date=December 29, 2009 | access-date=December 30, 2009 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20091231154903/http://www.vecernji.hr/vijesti/mesic-bandic-laze-bandic-mesic-je-malo-ostario-je-zaboravio-clanak-73129 | archive-date=December 31, 2009 | url-status=live | df=mdy-all }}</ref> He also suggested there could be one debate held entirely in English, mocking Bandić since he previously claimed he speaks the language.<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.net.hr/vijesti/hrvatska/page/2009/12/28/0692006.html | title=Mogli bi održati raspravu kandidata na engleskom | publisher=Net.hr | date=December 28, 2009 | access-date=December 30, 2009 | archive-url=https://archive.today/20120905175059/http://www.net.hr/vijesti/hrvatska/page/2009/12/28/0692006.html | archive-date=September 5, 2012 | url-status=dead | df=mdy-all }}</ref> Bandić responded saying he would be glad to attend that debate only if Mesić was moderating it, referring to the fact that the president himself was also not an English speaker. He also called the president an 'old man' saying it was only natural he forgot about the help he provided him during his two campaigns.<ref>{{cite web | url=http://izbori.dnevnik.hr/clanak/milan_bandic/mesic-revizija-donacija-je-dostupna-i-to-na-hrvatskom.html | title=Mesić Bandiću: Lažeš; Bandić Mesiću: Ostario si | publisher=[[Nova TV (Croatia)|Nova TV]] | date=December 29, 2009 | access-date=December 30, 2009 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20110721100646/http://izbori.dnevnik.hr/clanak/milan_bandic/mesic-revizija-donacija-je-dostupna-i-to-na-hrvatskom.html | archive-date=July 21, 2011 | url-status=dead | df=mdy-all }}</ref>

[[File:Josipovic volunteers.jpg|thumb|250px|Volunteers for the Josipović campaign]]

On 29 December Josipović gave a speech on an SDP convention held in [[Rijeka]] where he said that with the following presidential election the political map of Croatia would change forever and that by the [[2011 Croatian parliamentary election|next parliamentary election]] Croatia would be colored red, referring to his party's official colour being red.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.nacional.hr/clanak/74672/josipovic-sdp-ovom-pobjedom-cemo-zacrveniti-cijelu-hrvatsku |title=Josipović: SDP-ovom pobjedom ćemo zacrveniti cijelu Hrvatsku |trans-title=Josipović: SDP's victory will turn the entire Croatia red |work=[[Nacional (weekly)|Nacional]] |date=30 December 2009 |access-date=23 July 2012 |archive-date=24 March 2012 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120324210420/http://www.nacional.hr/clanak/74672/josipovic-sdp-ovom-pobjedom-cemo-zacrveniti-cijelu-hrvatsku }}</ref> Bandić did not waste time and the next day attacked Josipović arguing that the next president should not be biased once again repeating his claim that Josipović is nothing more than a pawn of Zoran Milanović who would work in his benefit if he should win.<ref>{{cite web | url=http://izbori.dnevnik.hr/clanak/milan_bandic/bandic-opet-prozvao-josipovica-sutra-cu-podastrijeti-dokumentaciju.html?&page=6&p_all_items=29 | title=Bandić opet prozvao Josipovića: 'Sutra ću dokazati' | publisher=[[Nova TV (Croatia)|Nova TV]] | date=January 2, 2010 | access-date=January 3, 2010 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20110721100736/http://izbori.dnevnik.hr/clanak/milan_bandic/bandic-opet-prozvao-josipovica-sutra-cu-podastrijeti-dokumentaciju.html?&page=6&p_all_items=29 | archive-date=July 21, 2011 | url-status=dead | df=mdy-all }}</ref> The prime minister [[Jadranka Kosor]] also criticized Josipović's remarks as unfitting.<ref>{{cite web | url=http://izbori.dnevnik.hr/clanak/kosor-hrvatska-se-nece-zacrvenjeti.html | title=Kosor: Hrvatska se neće zacrvenjeti! | publisher=[[Nova TV (Croatia)|Nova TV]] | date=December 31, 2009 | access-date=January 3, 2010 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20110721100803/http://izbori.dnevnik.hr/clanak/kosor-hrvatska-se-nece-zacrvenjeti.html | archive-date=July 21, 2011 | url-status=dead | df=mdy-all }}</ref>

The first two second-round debates were held on the same evening, 30 December, the first on [[Croatian Radiotelevision|HRT]] starting a couple of minutes after 8&nbsp;p.m., and the second on [[Nova TV (Croatia)|Nova TV]] starting a couple of minutes before 10&nbsp;p.m. During the debates Josipović emphasized his untarnished political career as well as his knowledge of the law and the [[Constitution of Croatia|Constitution]]. He defended himself from attacks made by Bandić earlier in the week that he was one of those responsible for writing criminal indictments against Croatia's generals during the [[Croatian War of Independence|war]], denouncing the claims as flat-out lies, saying that he offered legal aid to captured Croatian soldiers during the war.<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.hrt.hr/index.php?id=275&tx_ttnews%5Btt_news%5D=58189&tx_ttnews%5BbackPid%5D=274&cHash=0f9eb1b778 | title=Josipović i Bandić – Tko je na čijem "daljinskom"? | publisher=[[Croatian Radiotelevision|HRT]] | date=December 30, 2009 }}{{Dead link|date=April 2019 |bot=InternetArchiveBot |fix-attempted=yes }}</ref>

The most direct attack by Bandić on Josipović came at the very end of the first debate when he accused him of damaging the city of Zagreb in 1998 by allegedly abusing his position as the head of the oversight board of a savings bank ''Zlatica''<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.jutarnji.hr/bandic--josipovic-je-gurnuo-ruku-u-dzep-moje-punice-i-drugih-siromaha/447524/ | title=Bandić: Josipović je gurnuo ruku u džep moje punice i drugih siromaha | publisher=[[Jutarnji list]] | date=January 2, 2010 | access-date=January 3, 2010 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20100105020832/http://www.jutarnji.hr/bandic--josipovic-je-gurnuo-ruku-u-dzep-moje-punice-i-drugih-siromaha/447524 | archive-date=January 5, 2010 | url-status=live | df=mdy-all }}</ref> to make a series of financial maneuvers that enabled him to collect his deposit of 138,000 [[Deutsche Marks]] from the bank ''Komercijalna banka'' that had been blocked and later went bankrupt. Bandić cited a court ruling from 2006 that had invalidated those maneuvers.<ref>{{cite web | url = http://www.net.hr/vijesti/hrvatska/page/2010/01/05/0071006.html | title = Oštra završnica – Bandić Zlaticom 'kopa jamu' Josipoviću | language = hr | work = Net.hr | date = January 5, 2010 | access-date = January 7, 2010 | archive-url = https://web.archive.org/web/20111001024414/http://www.net.hr/vijesti/hrvatska/page/2010/01/05/0071006.html | archive-date = October 1, 2011 | url-status = live | df = mdy-all }}</ref> Josipović defended himself saying that was merely a civil case which he was not even a part of and that he did not commit any illegal actions.<ref>{{cite web | url=http://izbori.dnevnik.hr/clanak/ivo_josipovic/josipovic-bandic-nudi-blato-iz-kojeg-je-izasla-batina-za-radzenovica.html | title=Bandić priča o moralu, a razveo se zbog dva stana | publisher=[[Nova TV (Croatia)|Nova TV]] | date=January 2, 2009 | access-date=January 3, 2010 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20110721100820/http://izbori.dnevnik.hr/clanak/ivo_josipovic/josipovic-bandic-nudi-blato-iz-kojeg-je-izasla-batina-za-radzenovica.html | archive-date=July 21, 2011 | url-status=dead | df=mdy-all }}</ref> Josipović also had to defend his [[damaging quotation]] that Croatia would be coloured red by the next election, saying that it was only natural for a political party to be ambitious saying he does not consider the remarks to be unfitting repeating once again that, if elected, he would be the president of all citizens.<ref>{{cite web | url=http://izbori.dnevnik.hr/clanak/vijesti/josipovic-ocito-nema-kapaciteta-dobiti-izbore.html | title=Na sučeljavanju i Bandić i Josipović otkrili slabosti | publisher=[[Nova TV (Croatia)|Nova TV]] | date=December 31, 2009 | access-date=January 3, 2010 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20110721101019/http://izbori.dnevnik.hr/clanak/vijesti/josipovic-ocito-nema-kapaciteta-dobiti-izbore.html | archive-date=July 21, 2011 | url-status=dead | df=mdy-all }}</ref>

The issue of whom Ivo Sanader supports unexpectedly escalated when Sanader announced he was returning to active politics at a Sunday, January 3 press conference,<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.slobodnadalmacija.hr/Hrvatska/tabid/66/articleType/ArticleView/articleId/85943/Default.aspx | title=Sanader: Vraćam se, HDZ je loše vođen; Kosorica šuti, Bebić uz Ivu | publisher=[[Slobodna Dalmacija]] | date=January 3, 2010 | access-date=January 5, 2010 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120404132053/http://www.slobodnadalmacija.hr/Hrvatska/tabid/66/articleType/ArticleView/articleId/85943/Default.aspx | archive-date=April 4, 2012 | url-status=live | df=mdy-all }}</ref> which resulted in a blitz uproar among the coalition partners, and subsequently his ejection from the HDZ party. President Mesić attacked Bandić saying the former prime minister returned to support him, trying to once again link Bandić to the most unpopular politician in the country.<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.tportal.hr/vijesti/hrvatska/49999/Sanader-povratkom-pomaze-Bandicu.html | title=Sanader povratkom pomaže Bandiću | publisher=T-portal.hr | date=January 3, 2010 | access-date=January 5, 2010 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20110610231059/http://www.tportal.hr/vijesti/hrvatska/49999/Sanader-povratkom-pomaze-Bandicu.html | archive-date=June 10, 2011 | url-status=live | df=mdy-all }}</ref> Bandić denied such claims calling them lies and distractions and once again accused Josipović of being a pawn of Zoran Milanović.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.nacional.hr/clanak/75031/bandic-nikada-ne-bi-postupio-kao-sanader-josipovic-povratak-zbog-bandica |title=Bandić: Nikada ne bi postupio kao Sanader; Josipović: Povratak zbog Bandića |trans-title=Bandić: I would never follow example of Sanader; Josipović: Returning because of Bandić |publisher=[[Nacional (weekly)|Nacional]] |date=4 January 2010 |author=Martina Čizmić |access-date=23 July 2012 |archive-date=24 March 2012 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120324210427/http://www.nacional.hr/clanak/75031/bandic-nikada-ne-bi-postupio-kao-sanader-josipovic-povratak-zbog-bandica }}</ref> At the same time, Bandić's ally [[Željko Kerum]] publicly stated that Ivo Sanader would be an "ideal president",<ref>{{cite web | url = http://www.net.hr/vijesti/hrvatska/page/2010/01/01/0213006.html | title = A Bandić?! – Kerum: Sanader bi bio idealan predsjednik | work = Net.hr | date = January 1, 2010 | language = hr | access-date = January 7, 2010 | archive-url = https://web.archive.org/web/20111001024406/http://www.net.hr/vijesti/hrvatska/page/2010/01/01/0213006.html | archive-date = October 1, 2011 | url-status = live | df = mdy-all }}</ref> but afterwards he backtracked somewhat, while repeating his well-known attitude on how the media is biased against him and Bandić.<ref>{{cite web | url = http://www.slobodnadalmacija.hr/Split/tabid/72/articleType/ArticleView/articleId/86221/Default.aspx | work = [[Slobodna Dalmacija]] | language = hr | title = Kerum: Ne dolazi u obzir da Sanadera primim u moju stranku; HNK Bandić dobio besplatno od gradonačelnika | date = January 5, 2010 | access-date = January 7, 2010 | archive-url = https://web.archive.org/web/20120404132214/http://www.slobodnadalmacija.hr/Split/tabid/72/articleType/ArticleView/articleId/86221/Default.aspx | archive-date = April 4, 2012 | url-status = live | df = mdy-all }}</ref>

Milan Bandić heavily used religion as an issue in the campaign, calculating that Josipović's [[agnosticism]] would be a turn-off for a largely [[Catholic]] country as Croatia. He constantly repeated the only one he fears is God and that he was raised as a true believer and a humble [[Christians|Christian]], also making claims that he has the support of the [[Catholic Church]].<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.index.hr/vijesti/clanak.aspx?id=468595 | title=Milan Bandić: Imam podršku Katoličke crkve! | publisher=Index.hr | date=January 5, 2010 | access-date=January 5, 2010 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20121017003831/http://www.index.hr/vijesti/clanak.aspx?id=468595 | archive-date=October 17, 2012 | url-status=live | df=mdy-all }}</ref> Josipović largely ignored Bandić's attempts saying he would be the president of all Croatians no matter their religious beliefs. The incumbent president Stjepan Mesić was elected twice despite his [[atheism]].<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.nacional.hr/clanak/55298/zivot-bez-boga-i-vraga-u-katolickoj-hrvatskoj |title=Život bez Boga i vraga u katoličkoj Hrvatskoj |trans-title=Life without the God or the Devil in Catholic Croatia |publisher=[[Nacional (weekly)|Nacional]] |date=24 March 2009 |author=Robert Bajruši |language=hr |access-date=23 July 2012 |archive-date=19 January 2012 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120119122456/http://www.nacional.hr/clanak/55298/zivot-bez-boga-i-vraga-u-katolickoj-hrvatskoj }}</ref> However, the Bandić campaign used all tactics to force the issue, even distributing fliers in front of churches after the Sunday mass across the country urging believers to choose between the cross and a red star, referencing communism.<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.index.hr/vijesti/clanak.aspx?id=468339 | title=Maloljetnici nakon mise u Petrinji dijele letke na kojima blate Josipovića i uzdižu Bandića | publisher=Index.hr | date=January 4, 2010 | access-date=January 5, 2010 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20100110025401/http://www.index.hr/vijesti/clanak.aspx?id=468339 | archive-date=January 10, 2010 | url-status=live | df=mdy-all }}</ref>

[[File:Milan bandić poster.JPG|thumb|250px|One of the posters of the Bandić campaign. The message roughly translates: 'Choose: A party or an independent president?' A picture of a remote-control is shown in the lower-left corner referencing Bandić's accusation that Josipović is a pawn on a remote-control of his party]]

Eventually, Josipović responded to the other side's [[discrediting tactic]]s based on religion as well as the savings fund affair by raising the issue of how Bandić had divorced his wife in 1996 and because of that managed to buy out another apartment from the government with a discount,<ref>{{cite web | url = http://www.index.hr/vijesti/clanak.aspx?id=248861 | title = Bandić se 1996. razveo zbog otkupa stana? | language = hr | work = Index.hr | date = February 10, 2005 | access-date = January 7, 2010 | archive-url = https://web.archive.org/web/20090602233259/http://www.index.hr/vijesti/clanak.aspx?id=248861 | archive-date = June 2, 2009 | url-status = live | df = mdy-all }}</ref> claiming Bandić violated the most sacred sacrament of marriage with the intent of making profit.<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.net.hr/vijesti/hrvatska/page/2010/01/02/0058006.html | title=Bandić se razveo da bi mogao otkupiti stanove | publisher=Net.hr | date=January 2, 2010 | access-date=January 5, 2010 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20111001024335/http://www.net.hr/vijesti/hrvatska/page/2010/01/02/0058006.html | archive-date=October 1, 2011 | url-status=dead | df=mdy-all }}</ref> Bandić responded in outrage saying he went through great emotional pain during his divorce saying Josipović was not a man unless he apologized.<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.tportal.hr/vijesti/hrvatska/50110/Mercep-napao-Josipoviceve-branitelje.html | title=Uvrijedio mi je suprugu | publisher=T-portal.hr | date=January 4, 2010 | access-date=January 4, 2010 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20110610230902/http://www.tportal.hr/vijesti/hrvatska/50110/Mercep-napao-Josipoviceve-branitelje.html | archive-date=June 10, 2011 | url-status=live | df=mdy-all }}</ref>

On 3 January the third debate took place, hosted by [[RTL Televizija]]. The main topics were the return of former prime minister Ivo Sanader to the political scene, the economy, taxes and foreign relations, especially with [[Slovenia]]. Bandić once again repeated he was a man of work who would do anything for the people, while Josipović demonstrated his knowledge of law and foreign policy.<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.rtl.hr/rtl-duel-video-5399 | title=RTL duel | publisher=[[RTL Televizija]] | date=January 3, 2010 | access-date=January 4, 2010 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20100106022438/http://www.rtl.hr/rtl-duel-video-5399 | archive-date=January 6, 2010 | url-status=live | df=mdy-all }}</ref> On the next day, the results of a second set of election polls were published, showing Bandić made some gains, but Josipović's support was mostly unchanged.<ref name="mediametar4jan"/><ref name="promocijaplus4jan"/>

The Josipović campaign released a list of 20 Croatian generals who allegedly supported him in the second round.<ref name="javno.com">{{cite web |url=http://www.javno.com/hr-hrvatska/ademi-blaskic-i-kotromanovic-podrzali-josipovica_288155 |title=Ademi, Blaškić i Kotromanović podržali Josipovića |work=Javno.hr |language=hr |date=December 30, 2009 |access-date=2009-12-31 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20100122204816/http://www.javno.com/hr-hrvatska/ademi-blaskic-i-kotromanovic-podrzali-josipovica_288155 |archive-date=January 22, 2010 |url-status=live |df=mdy-all }}</ref> This endorsement was subsequently used in campaign advertisements by Josipović. One of these generals, Nojko Marinović, denied any participation in the endorsement, calling it a "coarse manipulation".<ref>{{cite web | url = http://www.slobodnadalmacija.hr/Hrvatska/tabid/66/articleType/ArticleView/articleId/86458/Default.aspx | title = Umirovljeni general Marinović: Nisam za Josipovića, moj kandidat je bio Tuđman | work = [[Slobodna Dalmacija]] | language = hr | date = January 6, 2010 | access-date = 2010-01-06 | archive-url = https://web.archive.org/web/20120404132200/http://www.slobodnadalmacija.hr/Hrvatska/tabid/66/articleType/ArticleView/articleId/86458/Default.aspx | archive-date = April 4, 2012 | url-status = live | df = mdy-all }}</ref>
Petar Janjić-Tromblon was also listed and he released a statement denying his support, saying he "doesn't want to be part of their games".<ref>{{cite web | url = http://www.javno.com/hr-hrvatska/janjic-tromblon--nisam-dao-potporu-josipovicu_288254 | title = Demantij branitelja – Janjić-Tromblon: Nisam dao potporu Josipoviću | work = Javno.com | date = December 31, 2009 | language = hr | access-date = January 7, 2010 | archive-url = https://archive.today/20130126163901/http://www.javno.com/hr-hrvatska/janjic-tromblon--nisam-dao-potporu-josipovicu_288254 | archive-date = January 26, 2013 | url-status = live | df = mdy-all }}</ref> The name of Tihomir Blaškić was also floated in the media in this context. Josipović was confronted about it during the third debate, and he claimed that the disavowals were made because of peer pressure.
The Bandić campaign also released their own list of associations of Croatian defenders who allegedly supported him in the second round,<ref name="bandic-veterans"/> including the Association of the 105th Brigade of the [[Croatian National Guard]], but the war-time commander of the 105th Brigade of the [[Croatian Army]] Stjepan Ivanić came forward to state that their association was both named and listed wrongly and said that their members were "appalled by the disinformation".<ref>{{cite web | url = http://www.vecernji.hr/vijesti/udruga-105-brigade-trazimo-demantij-bandica-clanak-76100 | title = Udruga 105. brigade: Tražimo demantij od Bandića | language = hr | work = [[Večernji list]] | date = January 7, 2010 | access-date = January 7, 2010 | archive-url = https://web.archive.org/web/20100110052438/http://www.vecernji.hr/vijesti/udruga-105-brigade-trazimo-demantij-bandica-clanak-76100 | archive-date = January 10, 2010 | url-status = live | df = mdy-all }}</ref>

The Bandić campaign created a [[negative campaign]] television ad that used a recording of Josipović's words, but after the Josipović campaign complained, the State Election Committee banned it as a violation of campaign rules, while Bandić campaign complained of censorship.<ref>{{cite web | url = http://www.hrt.hr/index.php?id=275&tx_ttnews%5Btt_news%5D=58724&tx_ttnews%5BbackPid%5D=274&cHash=616c3c3a8d | title = Zabranjen Bandićev spot | language = hr | work = [[HINA]]/[[Croatian Radiotelevision]] | date = January 6, 2009 }}{{Dead link|date=April 2019 |bot=InternetArchiveBot |fix-attempted=yes }}</ref> They eventually released a modified version of the same ad, just avoiding the use of Josipović's own voice.

The January 7 debate on Nova TV was held at 21:45, moderated once again by Mislav Bago. The two candidates had a somewhat more intense exchange regarding most issues previously discussed in the campaign. They once again compared tenure in the [[League of Communists of Croatia]] and SDP, their personal properties as well as moral values. Josipović called on Bandić to compare their physical and stock properties in court, which the latter refused. There was some talk of endorsements, and some reflections on [[talking point]]s. They finished in a more cordial tone with the mention of future private visits as well as family pets.

The last debate occurred on January 8 on HRT, moderated by Branimir Bilić. Most common topics were covered once again, ending with some larger themes of international politics such as global warming and the inequality of the third world.

