** [[Marko Perković Thompson]],<ref name="milanbandic.com 511">{{cite web|url=http://www.milanbandic.com/vijesti/511-potpora-milanu-bandicu-od-zvonka-busica-i-thompsona.html |title=Potpora Milanu Bandiću od Zvonka Bušića i Thompsona |date=December 31, 2009 |work=milanbandic.com |language=hr |access-date=2010-01-10 |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20100105151858/http://www.milanbandic.com/vijesti/511-potpora-milanu-bandicu-od-zvonka-busica-i-thompsona.html |archive-date=January 5, 2010 }}</ref> [[Zvonko Bušić]],<ref name="milanbandic.com 511"/> [[Zlatko Sudac]]<ref>{{cite web |author=Tomislav Čadež |url=http://www.jutarnji.hr/jedan-stozer-kao-soping-centar--drugi-kao-crkva/466719/ |title=Jedan stožer kao šoping centar, drugi kao crkva |work=[[Jutarnji list]] |date=7 January 2010 |language=hr |access-date=2010-05-14 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20100113022043/http://www.jutarnji.hr/jedan-stozer-kao-soping-centar--drugi-kao-crkva/466719/ |archive-date=13 January 2010 |url-status=live |df=dmy-all }}</ref>

==== Notable abstentions ====

The Croatian Democratic Union (HDZ) stated that they will not endorse any candidate in the second round,<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.nacional.hr/clanak/74499/razocarana-premijerka-hdz-u-drugom-krugu-nece-podrzati-nikoga |work=[[Nacional (weekly)|Nacional]] |title=Razočarana premijerka: HDZ u drugom krugu neće podržati nikoga |language=hr |date=28 December 2009 |trans-title=Disappointed PM: HDZ will not endorse anyone in the runoff |access-date=23 July 2012 |archive-date=13 June 2011 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20110613180223/http://www.nacional.hr/clanak/74499/razocarana-premijerka-hdz-u-drugom-krugu-nece-podrzati-nikoga }}</ref> and have censored local branches that attempted to explicitly endorse Bandić. This happened to HDZ's mayor of [[Zadar]] Zvonimir Vrančić who first endorsed him<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.ezadar.hr/clanak/vrancic-podrzao-bandica | title=Vrančić podržao Bandića | publisher=ezadar.hr | date=December 29, 2009 | access-date=December 30, 2009 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20110727021148/http://www.ezadar.hr/clanak/vrancic-podrzao-bandica | archive-date=July 27, 2011 | url-status=live | df=mdy-all }}</ref> but later disclaimed official support,<ref name="hdz-unofficial">{{cite web | url = http://www.hrt.hr/index.php?id=275&tx_ttnews%5Btt_news%5D=58195&tx_ttnews%5BbackPid%5D=274&cHash=79ff986cd2 | title = HDZ-ovi odbori posipavaju se pepelom | language = hr | work = [[Croatian Radiotelevision]] | date = December 30, 2009 }}{{Dead link|date=April 2019 |bot=InternetArchiveBot |fix-attempted=yes }}</ref> and also to the HDZ branch of [[Makarska]]<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.javno.com/hr-hrvatska/makarski-hdz-podupro-milana-bandica_288065 |title=Makarski HDZ podupro Milana Bandića – Hrvatska |publisher=Javno |date=December 29, 2009 |access-date=2009-12-31 |archive-url=https://archive.today/20120908212757/http://www.javno.com/hr-hrvatska/makarski-hdz-podupro-milana-bandica_288065 |archive-date=September 8, 2012 |url-status=live |df=mdy-all }}</ref> which also retracted their support under threat of sanction.<ref name="hdz-unofficial"/>

The [[Catholic Church in Croatia]] claimed that they're neutral in this; the [[Croatian Bishops' Conference]] states that they never endorse anyone. But, there are some signs of subtle pro-Bandić attitude: Croatian archbishop [[Josip Bozanić]] was visited by Milan Bandić in the Archbishop's office on January 2.<ref>{{cite web | url = http://www.vecernji.hr/vijesti/kaptol-tvrdi-da-je-neutralan-ali-bozanic-ipak-prima-bandica-clanak-74316 | work = [[Večernji list]] | language = hr | title = Signal vjernicima – Kaptol tvrdi da je neutralan, ali Bozanić ipak prima Bandića | date = January 1, 2010 | access-date = January 2, 2010 | archive-url = https://web.archive.org/web/20100103104621/http://www.vecernji.hr/vijesti/kaptol-tvrdi-da-je-neutralan-ali-bozanic-ipak-prima-bandica-clanak-74316 | archive-date = January 3, 2010 | url-status = live | df = mdy-all }}</ref> The editor of the official church gazette ''[[Glas Koncila]]'' Ivan Miklenić, otherwise known as a vocal critic of President Mesić, did not endorse any candidate and instead expressed disappointment with both candidates,<ref>{{cite web | url = http://www.net.hr/vijesti/hrvatska/page/2009/12/29/0359006.html | title = Neuslišane molitve – Kaptolu nije po volji ni Bandić ni Josipović | work = Net.hr | date = December 29, 2009 | language = hr | access-date = January 5, 2010 | archive-url = https://archive.today/20120905202537/http://www.net.hr/vijesti/hrvatska/page/2009/12/29/0359006.html | archive-date = September 5, 2012 | url-status = live | df = mdy-all }}</ref> but later made statements that were interpreted to favor Bandić.<ref>{{cite news | newspaper = [[Večernji list]] | url = http://www.vecernji.hr/vijesti/glas-koncila-okrenuo-plocu-podrzava-milana-bandica-clanak-75469 | title = Katolici neka glasuju koga su biskupi preporučili Glas Koncila okrenuo ploču i podržava Milana Bandića | language = hr | date = January 5, 2010 | access-date = January 13, 2010 | archive-url = https://web.archive.org/web/20100108130144/http://www.vecernji.hr/vijesti/glas-koncila-okrenuo-plocu-podrzava-milana-bandica-clanak-75469 | archive-date = January 8, 2010 | url-status = live | df = mdy-all }}</ref> During the campaign, numerous minor violations related to Church members were observed by GONG, in favor of Bandić.<ref>{{cite web | url = http://www.vecernji.hr/vijesti/gong-crkva-krsila-izbornu-sutnju-sugerirajuci-glasovanje-bandica-clanak-76965 | title = Drugi krug predsjedničkih izbora – GONG: Crkva kršila izbornu šutnju sugerirajući glasovanje za Bandića | date = January 10, 2010 | language = hr | work = Večernji list | access-date = January 10, 2010 | archive-url = https://web.archive.org/web/20100112130221/http://www.vecernji.hr/vijesti/gong-crkva-krsila-izbornu-sutnju-sugerirajuci-glasovanje-bandica-clanak-76965 | archive-date = January 12, 2010 | url-status = live | df = mdy-all }}</ref>

Many first-round candidates endorsed the second-round candidates, but some made public statements regarding the second round but did not endorse. [[Dragan Primorac]] made several public statements - he initially tried to stay completely neutral,<ref name="tportal-jutarnji-endorsements"/> but later released one where he listed some characteristics of the future president that he would want, without naming a candidate, but focusing on the fight against corruption. The reception was mixed – ''[[Večernji list]]'' said he chose no one,<ref>{{cite web | url = http://www.vecernji.hr/vijesti/primorac-ne-podrzava-ni-bandica-ni-josipovica-clanak-73379 | title = Primorac ne podržava ni Bandića ni Josipovića | work = [[Večernji list]] | language = hr | date = December 29, 2009 | access-date = January 9, 2010 | archive-url = https://web.archive.org/web/20100101063545/http://www.vecernji.hr/vijesti/primorac-ne-podrzava-ni-bandica-ni-josipovica-clanak-73379 | archive-date = January 1, 2010 | url-status = live | df = mdy-all }}</ref> while ''[[Jutarnji list]]'' said that he chose Josipović, reading between the lines.<ref>{{cite web | url = http://www.jutarnji.hr/dragan-primorac-dao-podrsku-ivi-josipovicu/437882/ | title = Drugi krug izbora – Dragan Primorac dao podršku Ivi Josipoviću | work = [[Jutarnji list]] | language = hr | date = December 29, 2009 | access-date = January 9, 2010 | archive-url = https://web.archive.org/web/20100117014535/http://www.jutarnji.hr/dragan-primorac-dao-podrsku-ivi-josipovicu/437882/ | archive-date = January 17, 2010 | url-status = live | df = mdy-all }}</ref> The Josipović campaign later decided to include Primorac in their endorsement list<ref name="josipovic-endorsement-list">{{cite web | url = http://josipovic.net/ostalo/popis-podrske-ivi-josipovicu/ | title = Popis podrške Ivi Josipoviću | work = Josipovic.net | language = hr | date = January 8, 2010 | access-date = January 9, 2010 | archive-url = https://web.archive.org/web/20110819031201/http://josipovic.net/ostalo/popis-podrske-ivi-josipovicu/ | archive-date = August 19, 2011 | url-status = live | df = mdy-all }}</ref> and Primorac did not seem to come forward with a public rebuttal. On the other hand, [[Josip Jurčević]] made a late public statement telling voters to void their ballot.<ref>{{cite web | url = http://www.javno.com/hr-hrvatska/jurcevic-ne-podrzava-ni-bandica-ni-josipovica_289021 | title = Poništite listić – Jurčević ne podržava ni Bandića ni Josipovića | work = Javno.com | language = hr | date = January 7, 2010 | access-date = January 9, 2010 | archive-url = https://archive.today/20130208094150/http://www.javno.com/hr-hrvatska/jurcevic-ne-podrzava-ni-bandica-ni-josipovica_289021 | archive-date = February 8, 2013 | url-status = live | df = mdy-all }}</ref>

